00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:27,632
It's just we have to download Visual Studio Community first and then enable some settings and frameworks within Visual Studio Community.

252
00:21:27,854 --> 00:21:33,700
The reason why is because while the AI can write the C, it still needs a way to compile it.

253
00:21:33,966 --> 00:21:38,592
And it compiles Unreal C code through Visual Studio Community.

254
00:21:38,862 --> 00:21:41,312
So you want to go ahead and download the latest version.

255
00:21:41,486 --> 00:21:45,632
Specifically, it's not Visual Studio Code, which people get mixed up on.

256
00:21:45,872 --> 00:21:50,660
It is the actual Visual Studio with the purple icon, not the blue one.

257
00:21:51,086 --> 00:21:57,540
If you are installing Visual Studio for the first time, then it will ask you what frameworks or code bases you want to install with it.

258
00:21:57,712 --> 00:22:04,032
If you already have Visual Studio installed, then click on modify through the installer so you can pick those frameworks.

259
00:22:04,142 --> 00:22:16,112
Now specifically, you want .NET Multiplatform App UI development enabled, net desktop development, desktop development with C, and game development with C.

260
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:19,872
It even tells you in the description that this is meant for Unreal.

261
00:22:20,112 --> 00:22:21,636
Make sure those are enabled.

262
00:22:21,998 --> 00:22:26,432
And there are some additional code bases we need under game development with C.

263
00:22:27,598 --> 00:22:38,832
So under here, make sure C Profiling Tools is enabled, C build insights, Windows 11 SDK, 10.0.26 or newer.

264
00:22:39,278 --> 00:22:41,792
This is 261, so this is newer and will work.

265
00:22:42,032 --> 00:22:54,992
Visual Studio Tools for Unreal Engine, Visual Studio Debugger Tools for Unreal Engine, and just in case the Unreal Engine installer, although we already have the installer, this would just download that application for us automatically.

266
00:22:55,310 --> 00:23:01,632
So that is a lot of things we have to enable, but enabling all of these will make sure that Unreal Engine can compile C code.

267
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:03,792
And then select install or modify.

268
00:23:04,014 --> 00:23:09,060
To see if this is working, let's have it create a C class and then compile.

269
00:23:09,454 --> 00:23:12,512
But in order for it to compile, Unreal Engine has to be closed.

270
00:23:12,622 --> 00:23:14,020
So I'll go ahead and close it.

271
00:23:14,606 --> 00:23:22,752
And now within Claude, I'll tell it create a C class of just a sphere and compile Unreal.

272
00:23:22,832 --> 00:23:27,460
Let me know if everything is working or if I have to make any changes.

273
00:23:28,526 --> 00:23:34,788
So if we did forget something when we were enabling all those frameworks, then Claude will tell us what to enable.

274
00:23:35,726 --> 00:23:45,088
And this is the most unfortunate part about developing C for Unreal is that we constantly have to close a project for it to compile and then reopen it.

275
00:23:45,262 --> 00:23:49,284
Whenever we make a change, for the most part, we do have to close Unreal.

276
00:23:49,568 --> 00:24:01,488
And while it is technically possible, where when the AI is thinking about what C code to write and is writing the code, we can still be in the project and make edits when it's making those changes.

277
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:03,140
I don't recommend you do that.

278
00:24:03,566 --> 00:24:16,208
The reason why is because the AI is really smart, it is able to open up Unreal Engine by itself and then test different things, make sure everything compiles and catches bugs before you even know they exist.

279
00:24:16,526 --> 00:24:26,596
And then if we have our own instance of the editor open up, if we're making our own changes, then the AI will not double check its own work and will not open up Unreal by itself.

280
00:24:26,848 --> 00:24:31,684
So it's recommended that you do close Unreal whenever you make a change.

281
00:24:32,208 --> 00:24:37,572
And that is a huge hassle and it really does disrupt the flow when you're creating a project.

282
00:24:37,998 --> 00:24:39,876
So Epic Games is working on this.

283
00:24:40,398 --> 00:24:47,088
I do expect in a future version of the engine, you'll be able to prompt it to create code for you.

284
00:24:47,374 --> 00:24:49,568
And then we can still work in the engine.

285
00:24:49,728 --> 00:24:57,380
And if the AI needs to check something, then it will open up its own version of the editor that will not interfere with what we're doing.

286
00:24:57,728 --> 00:25:00,368
But that is a hassle for now.

287
00:25:00,558 --> 00:25:04,804
Just know that whenever you do make a change, close Unreal and reopen it when you're done.

288
00:25:05,008 --> 00:25:12,928
You can also tell the AI to remind it that it can open up the editor once it's done for us.

289
00:25:13,088 --> 00:25:17,888
That's how we don't have to open it up ourselves each time it is done compiling.

290
00:25:17,968 --> 00:25:23,488
And I'll show you how to do that in just a moment because now let's see if it did create that C class.

291
00:25:23,822 --> 00:25:33,488
Scrolling down here, if you do not see the C folder with the cog icon at the top right hand corner, come down here and make sure C is enabled.

292
00:25:33,568 --> 00:25:36,164
It's checked under C classes.

