295
00:25:45,678 --> 00:25:57,328
Oftentimes I will tell the AI that it has full permission to open up the project and to test to make sure that there are no errors and that everything is compiling correctly and that it got the basics of my task down.

296
00:25:57,774 --> 00:26:03,860
But even if you do not explicitly tell to test, the AI will by itself just open up on real.

297
00:26:04,334 --> 00:26:20,580
And you won't even see it open up on real because it likes to run programs in headless mode, which means that it can see the instance of the program it's running, but us, the editors, the humans, we're unable to see it, and that that's called running a program in headless mode.

298
00:26:20,782 --> 00:26:33,248
So even though Unreal Engine isn't open on your end, if you check the task manager, you might see that Unreal Engine, or if you're using Blender, is running right here, and that means that the AI is testing.

299
00:26:33,488 --> 00:26:42,128
Also, when the AI is running, when it is thinking, you can look at the drop downs and then see if it's taking any screenshots of Unreal Engine.

